# sky130A — open reference extraction deck for vyges-extract
#
# Two capacitance terms, calibrated separately and to very different standards. Read both
# notes before quoting a number from this deck.
#
# ── COUPLING (4th column) — calibrated on a SET of 10 blocks, 1 held out ───────────────
# Fit by `correlation/calibrate_coupling.py` against each block's own OpenLane OpenRCX SPEF:
# CF_UART_APB, counter, fft_top, humidistat_apb, mag_phase_apb, rv_plic_lite,
# spectrum_buffer, spi_host_lite, temp_sensor_apb, xbar_main — 35,682 nets. `fft_ctrl_tlul`
# (14,238 nets) was **held out entirely** and then scored: per-net median **1.04**, p10 0.83,
# p90 1.24, total 1.02. Every fitted block lands between 0.93 and 1.03.
# See correlation/ground-vs-coupling.md.
#
#   WARNING: the fitted coefficient is ~2.5x the ideal sidewall parallel-plate value for a
#   minimum-spaced pair, which on physics it should never exceed. That is the tell for a known
#   structural gap: this deck defines **no `interlayer` coefficients**, so the model computes
#   ZERO crossover (layer-to-layer) coupling and the lateral term is absorbing it. The fit
#   therefore reproduces OpenRCX's per-net coupling well while being non-physical
#   per-mechanism. It holds while the crossover-to-lateral ratio resembles these blocks — all
#   sky130 std-cell digital — and should NOT be trusted on a design with markedly different
#   layer usage. Adding interlayer terms and re-fitting both jointly is the next depth step.
#
#   li1 coupling is UNCALIBRATED: sky130 routing uses li1 only for via landings, so no li1
#   wire segment appears anywhere in the calibration set and nothing constrains it. met4/met5
#   coupling is met3's fitted value standing in (92 and 0 constraining nets respectively).
#
# ── GROUND CAP (3rd column) — calibrated on ONE block, and it shows ────────────────────
# Fit by `correlation/calibrate.py` on `counter` alone (50 nets), where it tracks OpenRCX to
# 0.997. On a dense block it runs **1.37x over** (per-net median 1.47), because `counter` is
# sparse and this deck has no shielding: field that terminates on a neighbour is field that
# did not terminate on ground, and a fixed fF/um cannot express that. The correlation between
# a net's coupling-to-ground ratio and its ground error is +0.94. `shield_k` exists for
# exactly this and is deliberately still unset — it multiplies OUR coupling, so it could not
# be fitted until the coupling column above was trustworthy. It now is; that is the next
# change to this file.
#
# ── RESISTANCE (2nd column) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Physical, from the sky130_fd_sc_hd nom tech LEF (RESISTANCE RPERSQ). Not calibrated against
# anything; an R correlation pass is separate.
#
# Calibrated to OpenRCX, a reference extractor — NOT to silicon. A sign-off / certified
# per-fab deck is silicon-correlated and NDA, and is never in this repo.
#
# layer  res(ohm/um)  cap(fF/um)  coupling(fF/um)  s_ref(um)
li1      12.8         0.060        0.030            0.17
met1      0.125       0.1259       0.21941          0.14
met2      0.125       0.1211       0.26618          0.14
met3      0.047       0.1371       0.26458          0.30
met4      0.047       0.1371       0.26458          0.30
met5      0.0285      0.1371       0.26458          1.60
via       9.3
couple_cutoff 2.0     # um — ignore lateral coupling beyond this gap
